This repository contains:

- patches/lf-studio.patch: modifications of NVIDIA's Sol-H3-Spark package in NVlabs/Sana
  (https://github.com/NVlabs/Sana, branch sol-engine, models/minimax_h3/Sol-H3-Spark, and one shared module,
  models/minimax_h3/super_acceleration/stage2/refiner_encoder_ablation_single_gpu.py). NVlabs/Sana is released by
  NVIDIA under the Apache License, Version 2.0. Each file the patch modifies is marked "Modified by lf-studio";
  docs/PATCH.md describes every change.
- Among the modified files, runtime/qwen_ops/media.py contains code derived from FastVideo
  (https://github.com/hao-ai-lab/FastVideo, by Hao AI Lab), licensed under the Apache License, Version 2.0.
- upscale/regen2k_job.py runs NVIDIA's Open-H3-Regenerate-2K (https://github.com/NVlabs/Sana, branch sol-engine,
  models/Open-H3-Regenerate-2K; not included) and contains code adapted from it: the LoRA merge arithmetic of
  adapters.StageMerger and the audio encode of pipeline.encode_silence. Apache License, Version 2.0. Its
  lean_forward is adapted from MiniMaxH3TransformerBlock.forward and MiniMaxH3AttnProcessor of Diffusers
  (https://github.com/huggingface/diffusers, 0.40.0, by The HuggingFace Team), Apache License, Version 2.0.
  upscale/fastload.py, with which it loads the weights, is a copy of runtime/fastload.py from
  patches/lf-studio.patch: a new file there, lf-studio's own code, not NVIDIA's.
- jobs/h3turbo_job.py (the experimental LightX2V Turbo) runs the modular MiniMax-H3 pipeline of Diffusers
  (https://github.com/huggingface/diffusers, 0.40.0, by The HuggingFace Team; Apache License, Version 2.0) with a
  LightX2V turbo LoRA, and contains code adapted from: PEFT's LoRA Linear forward (https://github.com/huggingface/peft,
  peft/tuners/lora/layer.py, by The HuggingFace Team; Apache License, Version 2.0), and the target modules, key names,
  step count and shift rules of LightX2V's Minimax-H3-Turbo reference inference
  (https://github.com/ModelTC/Minimax-H3-Turbo, inference_minimax_h3.py, by ModelTC; Apache License, Version 2.0).
- install/regen2k_weights.py contains code adapted from that package's download.py (the byte-range read of Sharp's
  AdaLN table, fetch_curve, and its file hashes), and install/constraints/regen2k-requirements.in starts from its
  requirements.txt. Apache License, Version 2.0.
- webui/index.html and bench/prompts/bench.jsonl contain example prompts taken or adapted from NVIDIA's
  Sol-H3-Spark (README.md and examples/prompts.jsonl), Apache License, Version 2.0. The prompt formats and section
  names in webui/index.html follow MiniMax's H3 prompt-writing guides
  (https://huggingface.co/MiniMaxAI/MiniMax-H3, docs/VIDEO_PROMPT_WRITING_GUIDE_base_en.md and
  docs/VIDEO_PROMPT_WRITING_GUIDE_ref_en.md).

Sol-H3-Spark and the Sol Video Inference Engine are by NVIDIA Research:
  Sol Video Inference Engine: Agent-Native Full-Stack Acceleration Framework for Efficient Video Generation.
  Yitong Li, Junsong Chen, Haopeng Li, Haozhe Liu, Jincheng Yu, Ligeng Zhu, Ping Luo, Song Han, Enze Xie.
  arXiv:2606.23743, 2026.

Open-H3-Regenerate-2K, which the experimental Upscale runs, is by NVIDIA Research
(https://nvlabs.github.io/Sana/Open-H3-Regenerate-2K/). NVIDIA asks users to cite the SoL-Refiner paper together
with that page:
  SoL-Refiner: Speed-of-Light One-Step Refinement for High-Resolution Video.
  Haozhe Liu, Tian Ye, Shuchen Xue, Yitong Li, Junsong Chen, Haopeng Li, Jincheng Yu, Duomin Wang, Ruihua Zhang,
  Lei Zhu, Song Han, Enze Xie. arXiv:2609.37969, 2026.
  Open-H3-Regenerate-2K: High-Resolution Video Refinement with Few-Step Diffusion. Sensen Gao, Haozhe Liu,
  Yitong Li, Haopeng Li, Tian Ye, Jia-Wang Bian, Song Han, Enze Xie. Project page, 2026.

LightX2V Turbo, the experimental second model, runs LightX2V's turbo LoRA for MiniMax-H3 by ModelTC
(https://huggingface.co/lightx2v/Minimax-h3-Turbo, https://github.com/ModelTC/Minimax-H3-Turbo; not included):
install/66-h3turbo.sh fetches the files at a pinned revision.

Not included here, obtained separately by the user, each under its own terms:

- Model weights: MiniMaxAI/MiniMax-H3, FastVideo/FastVideo-FastH3-4-step-Preview-v1-LoRA,
  lightx2v/Minimax-h3-Turbo, Comfy-Org/MiniMax-H3, Lightricks/LTX-2.5, LBH-123-AI/Minimax_h3_latent_Upscaler,
  Efficient-Large-Model/H3-to-LTX-Latent-Adapter, and for the experimental Upscale
  Efficient-Large-Model/Open-H3-Regenerate-2K (with the LightX2V Turbo and LMS Sharp LoRAs merged into its LoRA).
  See README.md, "Model terms".
- Source dependencies fetched by NVIDIA's prepare.py: FastVideo (Apache-2.0), FlashAttention (BSD-3-Clause),
  ComfyUI (GPL-3.0), Lightricks LTX-2 (LTX-2.x Community License), the LBH-123-AI H3 latent upscaler
  (https://github.com/LBH-123-AI/Comfyui_Minimax_h3_latent_Upscaler: MIT since 2026-09-17, commit 40316cf; the
  revision NVIDIA pins, d7c01b9, has no license file, and NVIDIA's notices say no license is declared).
- The H3 latent upscaler weights (LBH-123-AI/Minimax_h3_latent_Upscaler): the model card states Apache-2.0, in its
  text at the revision NVIDIA pins (13ccf95) and in its metadata since 2026-09-17.
- The Docker image built by install/60-qwen-image.sh: NVIDIA NGC PyTorch base image (NVIDIA terms) with ComfyUI
  (GPL-3.0). qwen-image/ contains only a Dockerfile and three small stub files; do not redistribute the built image.
